body: |-
  CRITICAL PATH STATUS (settled by TD-704, hardened by the design panels):
  DONE (app-independent, committed):
  1. LLM-judge — standalone cold instrument, foundation + live half + Aegis-cleared (TD-071; L-2026-08-12-011153).
  2. Fix B over-block false-KNOT — ripple-gate (TD-831; predict.ts bodyContested gate).
  3. Fix A Tier-0 false-CLEAN — surface-and-sample, no gate (TD-831; cli.ts disclaimer).
  5. Protocol amended (2 adversarial rounds) + LOCKED (TD-154).

  REMAINING (increasingly Expo-app-coupled):
  - Field-test RUNNER DRIVER: runJudgeEnforced exists; the 'walk Expo audit rows/KNOTs → cards' driver needs the actual run-data shape. Partially app-coupled. (T-2026-08-12-001.)
  - FROZEN BEHAVIORAL SMOKE ORACLE (protocol §4, the (A)-detector): the framework is app-independent; its ASSERTIONS probe THIS Expo app's config×code couplings → app-coupled.
  - SEEDED CONTROLS (A6 planted false-CLEAN, A11 known-GENUINE/OVER-BLOCK): fixture framework buildable; concrete seeds may mirror the app's patterns.
  - EXPO BACKLOG with overlap zones (protocol §3 driver): needs the actual Expo app.
  - THE RUN: needs the app + API keys + is the founder's operation; the witness-commit habit (T-2026-08-12-001) is part of the runbook.
  - Real-API regression case-13/case-20 (behind WARPLINE_JUDGE_LIVE): needs API access.

  The two HARDEST, most app-independent pieces (the instrument and the engine hardening) are done. The boundary now: the rest wants the actual Expo app in hand.

  Commits this arc: b85d56a8 (Track-A instruments) → 3862f450 (protocol lock) → 21d95b25/a92bfd21/346c9cf8 (judge) → 58cb76e9 (pre-fixes). All on warpline-surfaces, pushed to the (public) origin.
